  title: Rigveda
  text: The Rigveda, the oldest Veda, has 1,028 hymns in ten books, or mandalas, addressed to gods such as Indra, Agni and Soma. Passed down orally with great precision for centuries, its manuscripts are on UNESCO's Memory of the World register.
